  "summary_en": "Poland's November 2025 national AI development policy to 2030 from the Ministry of Digital Affairs. It sets five goals and indicators covering AI infrastructure (AI Factories), public administration, business, skills and trustworthy AI, aligned with the EU AI Act and Apply AI Strategy. Robotics and physical AI appear only marginally (autonomous vehicles, dual-use).",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Five goals to 2030 with measurable indicators, including 40 exaflops of AI compute and 34% SME AI adoption.",
   "Build AI Factories (Piast, Gaia), join EU AI Gigafactories, and develop PLLuM and Bielik language models.",
   "Set up regulatory sandboxes, with at least 50 firms a year testing in them.",
   "Critical infrastructure operators must comply with the AI Act, audit AI systems and report incidents; ISO/IEC 42001 and 27090 are to be adopted.",
   "Public list of AI systems used in administration; annual review and a coordination and funding system."
